# Cloudflare Tools for Kirby — Licence Agreement

Version 1.0
Copyright (c) 2026 Ian Hobbs. All rights reserved, except as granted below.

## About this Agreement

The source code of Cloudflare Tools for Kirby is publicly available, but the
plugin is **not free software**. You may use it without paying on
development and staging sites. Every public website that uses it needs a
paid licence.

By downloading, installing or using the Plugin, you agree to this Agreement.
If you don't agree, don't download, install or use the Plugin.

## Summary

This summary isn't legally binding; the numbered sections are.

- Try and build with the Plugin for free, for as long as you like, on
  Development Installations.
- Each Public Site needs one activation of a paid Licence Key. Your tier
  sets how many activations you have (for example 1, 5 or unlimited).
- A licence covers every release of the major version you bought (for
  example every 1.x release). A new major version may need an upgrade.
- You may change the code for your own sites. You may not resell it,
  redistribute it, or share or sell Licence Keys.
- The Plugin changes your Cloudflare configuration on your instructions.
  You are responsible for those changes.

## 1. Definitions

- **"We", "Us", "Our"**: Ian Hobbs, the licensor. Contact:
  <admin@ianhobbsmedia.com>.
- **"You", "Your"**: the person or organisation using the Plugin. If you buy
  a licence for a client's website, you are the licensee unless you transfer
  the licence to the client (section 5).
- **"Plugin"**: Cloudflare Tools for Kirby (Composer package
  `ianhobbs/kirby-cloudflare-tools`, registered in Kirby as
  `ianhobbs/cloudflare-tools`), including its source code, built assets,
  documentation and any updates We release, whether or not You have
  modified them.
- **"Website"**: a single Kirby installation, identified by its domain name
  and root directory (for example `https://example.com` or
  `https://shop.example.com`). Each domain, subdomain or root directory is a
  separate Website. Exception: domains that serve the same Kirby
  installation and content (for example one domain per language) count as
  one Website.
- **"Development Installation"**: a Website used only for development,
  testing or client review, and only reachable by a restricted group of
  people. Examples: a local computer, a private network, or a staging site
  behind a password.
- **"Public Site"**: any Website that isn't a Development Installation.
- **"Licence Key"**: the key We or Our reseller issue when You buy a
  licence. Its tier sets how many Public Sites it may be activated for.
- **"Activation"**: registering a Licence Key for one Public Site.

## 2. Free use on Development Installations

You may download, install, use, copy and modify the Plugin on Development
Installations without a Licence Key, with no time limit. This is for
evaluating the Plugin and for building, testing and previewing Websites.

## 3. Licence for Public Sites

3.1 Each Public Site that uses the Plugin needs one Activation of a valid
Licence Key. Activate the key as soon as the Website goes public.

3.2 When You buy a Licence Key, We grant You a non-exclusive, worldwide,
perpetual licence to use the Plugin on as many Public Sites as Your tier
allows. This licence is transferable only under section 5.

3.3 The licence covers every release of the major version You bought (for
example all 1.x releases), and You may keep using those releases for as
long as You like. A later major version may need a new licence or a paid
upgrade.

3.4 You may move an Activation from one Public Site to another, for example
when a site moves domain or is shut down. Deactivate it on the old site
first.

## 4. Source code and modifications

4.1 You may read, study and change the source code of the Plugin.

4.2 You may use modified versions on Your own Development Installations, and
on Public Sites that have an Activation. Modified versions remain subject to
this Agreement.

4.3 You may keep the Plugin, modified or not, in private repositories for
Your own Websites and those of Your clients.

4.4 Forking the repository on GitHub, as GitHub's terms allow, gives You no
rights beyond those in this Agreement.

## 5. Transfers

5.1 You may transfer a Licence Key, with all its Activations, to another
person or organisation, for example to the client who owns the Website. You
must tell Us about the transfer, and You lose the right to use that key.

5.2 You may not split a key's Activations between different licensees.

## 6. Restrictions

You may not:

- (a) sell, rent, lease, sublicense or redistribute the Plugin, modified or
  not, except as part of a Website it runs on, or as section 4.3 allows;
- (b) publish or distribute a modified version of the Plugin, including one
  with its licence checks removed;
- (c) share, publish, sell or give away Licence Keys, except by a transfer
  under section 5;
- (d) remove, disable or work around the Plugin's licence checks, notices or
  copyright notices on a Public Site that has no Activation; or
- (e) use the Plugin's source code to build a product that competes with it.

## 7. Licence checks and privacy

To activate and check a Licence Key, the Plugin may send the key and the
Website's domain name to Us or to Our payment and licensing provider. It
sends no other information for licensing. The Plugin sends Your Cloudflare
API credentials only to Cloudflare.

## 8. Your Cloudflare account and Kirby

8.1 The Plugin acts on Your Cloudflare account through the API token You
provide. Changes it makes on Your instructions (purges, settings, security
rules, DNS records, pausing Cloudflare) are Your responsibility. Use a token
limited to the permissions and zones You need.

8.2 Your use of Cloudflare is governed by Cloudflare's own terms. Kirby
needs its own licence from its publisher; this Agreement doesn't include
one.

## 9. Refunds

You may ask for a full refund within 30 days of buying a Licence Key. When
We refund a purchase, the licence for that key ends, and You must stop using
the Plugin on the Public Sites it was activated for, or buy a new key.

## 10. Termination

10.1 This Agreement ends automatically if You break it and don't put the
breach right within 14 days of Us telling You about it.

10.2 When it ends, You must stop using the Plugin on Public Sites.
Sections 6, 8, 11 and 12 continue after it ends.

## 11. Warranty and liability

11.1 The Plugin is provided "as is". We don't promise that it is free of
errors, or that it works with every version of Kirby, PHP or the Cloudflare
API.

11.2 Nothing in this Agreement excludes, restricts or modifies any
guarantee, right or remedy You have under the Australian Consumer Law, or
any other law, that cannot lawfully be excluded.

11.3 Where We are allowed to limit Our liability, it is limited, at Our
choice, to supplying the Plugin again or refunding what You paid for the
Licence Key.

11.4 To the extent the law allows, We are not liable for indirect or
consequential loss, including lost revenue, lost data, website downtime or
loss caused by changes to Your Cloudflare configuration.

